    "body": "**Scope update (user direction, 2026-11-11): make it an import toggle for the user on the import page.**\n\n- **Format:** `.camtools` entries may carry the tool body (the drawn holder profile, plus the built-in holder's name when it came from the holder library). It round-trips like a `.camproj` tool. Older files without it load unchanged. Export writes the holder body with each tool.\n- **Import page toggle:** the tool-library import dialog/page gets an option, e.g. **\"Import tool holders\"**.\n  - **On:** each tool keeps the holder body stored in the file.\n  - **Off:** tools come in with no holder body, keeping the conservative `holder_d`/`holder_len` cylinder (or the default holder), so the user can pick holders for their own machine.\n  - Show how many tools in the file carry a holder, so the choice is informed.\n  - Remember the setting per user, not as project state (cf. #877).\n- **MCP:** `import_tool_library` takes the same option (e.g. `holders: true|false`, default true).\n- **Undo:** the import stays one undoable command either way.\n\n**Done means:**\n- export then import with the toggle on keeps holder profiles bit-identical;\n- toggle off imports no holder bodies;\n- old files load unchanged;\n- the UI toggle is pinned by a structural test, and the MCP option by an app test.\n\nRelated: #799, and #899 (same import page).",
